<title>USA: Dickstein group cuts Hills Stores stake.</title>
<headline>Dickstein group cuts Hills Stores stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by investor Mark Dickstein said Wednesday it reduced its stake in Hills Stores Co to 2.2 percent or 226,803 common shares;</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it sold 383,700 shares of Hills Stores between January 6 and January 8 at prices ranging from $3.00 to $4.1180 a share.</p>
<p>The group previously held a 6.0 percent stake in the Canton, Mass., discount retailer.</p>
